I am still standing in the shop.
I do not pack the green coat into my bag.
I put the new coat on right away.
It is heavy and very warm.
Then I take the yellow hat.
I put the warm hat on too.
My thin jacket is now in the bag.
I am finally wearing a real winter coat now.
I walk to the exit and open the door.
Outside it is very cold.
An icy wind is blowing on the street.
I walk outside, but I am not freezing.
The wind is strong, but the thick coat protects me.
I smile, for I am very happy.
The cold weather is no longer a problem now.
For the first time in Berlin, I am truly warm.
I walk to the U-Bahn feeling satisfied.
Tomorrow I will wear the coat again.
